From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qmgr: BITS error descriptions, byte ranges, remote names, client certificates, clones

The rest of the BITS stubs:

- Error descriptions: IBackgroundCopyManager::GetErrorDescription and
  IBackgroundCopyError::GetErrorDescription describe BITS's own errors
  (our wording) and the system's and WinHTTP's (their message tables);
  GetErrorContextDescription describes the error's context; GetProtocol
  names the protocol of the file in error ("http" or "file").
- HTTP statuses: any 2xx is success (206 for a range); any other status
  is BITS's HTTP error 0x8019xxxx with the status code. Statuses BITS has
  no constant for (403, 500, ...) were taken as success.
- Byte ranges: AddFileWithRanges checks its ranges (in order, apart, of
  some length, BG_LENGTH_TO_EOF last; HTTP only) and the transfer asks for
  each range (Range header) and writes them one after another, as BITS
  does; GetFileRanges.
- SetRemoteName of a file not being or already transferred, checked as
  AddFile checks.
- Client certificates (by hash or by subject, in a system store of any
  location) are kept, read back and given to WinHTTP for the request;
  the job's SSL and redirect policy flags are applied to its requests.
- The jobs' and files' enumerators clone.

Wine's qmgr tests: no failures, as before.

Gate: test/bitsmore-gate.sh with test/bitsmore-server.py (64- and 32-bit).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_RANGES, SG_MUTANT_HTTP_ANY_OK (qmgr/file.c).
